Subject: [PATCH 17/69] fix(ui,ci): record message receive times in state
 updates and add delegate migration CI (#125)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* fix(ui,ci): record message receive times in state updates and add delegate migration CI

Message receive times were only recorded in apply_delta (subscription deltas),
but River subscribes with summary: None, so the node always sends UpdateData::State.
This meant receive times were never recorded and tooltip delays never showed.

Also fixes CI red (missing `gateway` field in NetworkArgs) and adds a CI workflow
to detect delegate WASM changes without corresponding LEGACY_DELEGATES migration entries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* chore: simplify CI and comment in PR #125

- Cache b3sum binary and skip reinstall when cached in delegate migration CI
- Condense receive-times comment to match style of nearby code

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix: address review feedback — skip receive times on initial sync, harden CI

- Only record receive times after initial sync is complete, avoiding
  false propagation delays for messages that arrived while offline
- Add cargo clean between base/PR builds to prevent incremental build
  artifacts from causing false negatives in delegate migration check
- Strengthen LEGACY_DELEGATES grep to require added lines (not just mentions)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix(ci): narrow check-wasm-sync trigger to exclude test files

The path trigger `contracts/room-contract/**` was matching test file
changes (e.g., test_utils.rs), causing false positives. Narrowed to
`contracts/room-contract/src/**` and `Cargo.toml` which are the only
paths that affect the compiled WASM.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

